export anchor ExhibitionCatalogueStyle:
    number: 89
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Exhibition catalogue
    idea: The dashboard is bound as an art catalogue of open spreads, with numbered plates for each project, catalogue entries on the facing page and wide calm margins that pair a book serif with a clean sans.
    base: light
    palette:
        table: #e7e5df, the surface behind the book
        page: #ffffff, every spread and the colophon
        plateGround: #f3efe7, plate backgrounds
        ink: #1b1b1b, text, rules and plate frames
        captionGrey: #616161, running heads, captions and folios
        rule: #d9d6cf, hairlines, never text
        vermilionInk: #a8321f, the primary button, the drop cap, overdue, Behind and focus
        vermilion: #c2412b, the Design plate and the this week fill
        prussian: #24476b, Engineering plates
        olive: #6d7436, the Research plate
        rose: #c98a8a, Marketing plates
        green: #2c6a3f, On track
        ochre: #8a5600, At risk
    type:
        Two stacks. The serif is Charter, Bitstream Charter, Sitka Text,
        Cambria, Iowan Old Style, Georgia, serif for the 54px greeting,
        32px page titles, 22px entry titles and 17px body with 1.6 line
        height, with italic ledes and dates. The sans is Avenir Next,
        Avenir, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, Arial at 300 for 64px figures
        tracked minus 0.03em, 13px plate captions, and 11px caps tracked
        0.14em for running heads, labels and statuses.
    layout:
        A slim header row on the grey table holds the brand with the italic
        line catalogue of the week, plain nav links with the current one
        underlined in vermilion, a boxed search, the New project button, a
        square bell and the user. Below sit three open book spreads, each a
        white two page sheet with a shaded gutter down the middle, 72px
        outer and 88px inner margins, a running head over a hairline on
        each page and a folio number at the foot. Spread one has the
        greeting with a vermilion drop cap essay and a diamond line saying
        4 tasks are overdue, facing The week in figures as a two by two
        table of light sans numbers with italic notes. Spread two has six
        plates in a two column grid, each a framed ground filled from the
        left to the percentage in the team colour with a black dot at the
        edge and a caption such as Plate 1, facing the catalogue with Cat.
        1 to 6 entries giving name, team, plate, due date, tasks and
        status. Spread three has a chronology on a ruled timeline facing
        Plate 7, a stepped line chart. Below 980px each spread becomes one
        column with its pages stacked.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 72px outer and 88px inner page margins, 48px under running heads and 36px between plates.
    density: Low. One subject per page, generous white space and long calm lines.
    corners: Square throughout.
    borders: 1px hairlines under running heads and between entries, and a 1px ink frame inside each plate.
    shadows: Each spread lifts off the table with a soft 40px shadow and a shaded gutter down its middle.
    icons:
        Small solid shapes with the caps word. On track is a filled
        circle, At risk a filled triangle, Behind a flat bar and overdue a
        diamond.
    focus: A 2px vermilion ink outline offset 3px. A focused field turns its border vermilion.
    tone: Curatorial and measured, such as Plates, Catalogue, Chronology, Cat. 4 and shown in plates 1 to 6.
